 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to peace officers at the video lottery gaming facility at the Aqueduct racetrack",
    "basePrintNo": "S3746",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3746-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1617-a, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3746\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to peace offi-\ncers at the video lottery gaming facility at the Aqueduct racetrack\n\nPURPOSE: To require the presence of peace officers at the Aqueduct race-\ntrack.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 1617-a of the tax law by adding a new subdivi-\nsion g to require the presence of peace officers at the Aqueduct race-\ntrack, pursuant to the approval of the gaming commission. The legis-\nlation stipulates that these peace officers are not authorized to carry,\npossess a firearm in the course of their duties.\n\nSection 2. The effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: Currently, Aqueduct casino employs security guards to\nensure the security of the public who attend the site and the employees\nwho work there. However, they are not authorized to make arrests but\nonly to detain an offender until the NYPD arrives. Other casinos such as\nEmpire City Casino, employs peace officers who can make arrests. With\nAqueduct employing peace officer with this authority, it will deter\nfuture instances of criminal activity and dissuade others who may choose\nto perpetrate crimes upon the public visiting the casino.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: Immediately.\n\n",
