    "lawCode": "Amd §1617-a, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3746A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to peace\nofficers at the video lottery gaming facility at the Aqueduct\nracetrack\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require the presence of peace officers at the Aqueduct racetrack.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 1617-a of the tax law by adding a new\nsubdivision g to require the presence of peace officers at the\nAqueduct racetrack, pursuant to the approval of the gaming commission.\nThe legislation stipulates that these peace officers are not\nauthorized to carry, possess a firearm in the course of their duties.\n\nSection 2. The effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, Aqueduct casino employs security guards to ensure the\nsecurity of the public who attend the site and the employees who work\nthere. However, they are not authorized to make arrests but only to\ndetain an offender until the NYPD arrives. Other casinos such as\nEmpire City Casino, employs peace officers who can make arrests. With\nAqueduct employing peace officer with this authority, it will deter\nfuture instances of criminal activity and dissuade others who may\nchoose to perpetrate crimes upon the public visiting the casino.\n\nLEGISLATIVE, HISTORY:\n\n2012: S. 3746 - Referred to Racing, Gaming and Wagering.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
